    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
